# trzy is a t released and then an sz, where czy is one sound; drzewo is a d
# and then a ż, where dżem is one. The phones are the same two in both,
# because the hard affricates are laid down as a stop and a fricative for want
# of codes of their own, and Italian times them identically. What tells a
# cluster is its release, so a stop laid down for the t or d of trz or drz is
# given a longer one than Italian's rule gave it -- added to Italian's rather
# than set, since Italian's own is not always ten.
#
# The letter rules mark such a stop `tense', which no consonant is and nothing
# else reads; the phone asked about is the one after variable 832. Reading
# the letters from there instead works only at the start of a word, the point
# before a phone further in being one the letters no longer share once the
# syllables have been made. How much longer is the ear's.
rule pol_ph_t_dur takes 1 from is_dur.obj
  afresh
  variable here word 832
  variable release half 2990
  call ital_ph_t_dur
  if answer is not 0
    give up
  end
  call ZZfence_null
  call lpta_loadp addr here
  call setscan_r 2
  if answer is 0
    call testFldeq 2 8 0
    if answer is 0
      add 10 to release
    end
  end
  match
end

rule pol_ph_d_dur takes 1 from is_dur.obj
  afresh
  variable here word 832
  variable release half 2990
  call ital_ph_d_dur
  if answer is not 0
    give up
  end
  call ZZfence_null
  call lpta_loadp addr here
  call setscan_r 2
  if answer is 0
    call testFldeq 2 8 0
    if answer is 0
      add 10 to release
    end
  end
  match
end
